# Milestone: M3
# Covers: an allocation-heavy strand sets vm->gc_pending (debt > threshold);
#         urbi_gc_slice is invoked at the next dispatch-loop safepoint of any
#         strand; GC slice runs and clears the pending flag (row 12 §4.4 —
#         gc_pending safepoint hook in dispatch_loop_until_yield).
#
# defer-to: M4 (no GC-managed cell allocations available from REPL at M3)
#
# Reason: triggering gc_pending from REPL urbiscript requires allocating enough
# GC-managed cells (UObject, UString) to exceed the gc_threshold.  At M3,
# the GC-managed cell types (UObject, UString, UList) land at M4/M5; the only
# allocations performed during REPL eval at M3 are closures and upvalue cells,
# which go through the VM's alloc_fn but are NOT tracked in gc_total_allocated
# (they are pre-GC bookkeeping, not GC-managed cells).  The GC slice mechanism
# itself is fully wired at M3 (gc_debt accumulation, urbi_gc_slice dispatch)
# and is covered by tests/unit/test_ugc_state_machine.c; the REPL-observable
# version must wait for M4 allocatable cell types.
#
# When M4 lands (UObject / UString as GC cells), implement this by:
#   var i = 0
#   while (i < 5000) { var s = String.new("x") | i = i + 1 }
#   -- verify gc_phase cycled and no OOM --
#   i
#   --- expected output ---
#   [00000001] 5000
